    "input": "search_document: Based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the clarification regarding your email verification timeline and the consequences of missing it:\n\n**1. Is it strictly 24 hours from registration?**\nYes. You are required to verify your email within **24 hours** of registration. If your email is not verified within this 24-hour window, your account will be **automatically suspended** [accounts].\n\n**2. Do you have to start the sign-up process over from scratch if you miss the window?**\nNo, you do not have to start over immediately. If your account is suspended due to the missed 24-hour window, you may **reactivate it by resending the verification link** [accounts].\n\n**3. What happens if you still don't verify?**\nIf the account remains unverified for **7 days** (from the initial registration), the account is **permanently deleted**, and any associated draft orders are canceled [accounts].\n\n**Summary of Steps to Avoid Issues:**\n*   Verify your email within 24 hours to avoid suspension [accounts].\n*   If you miss the 24-hour mark, your account suspends, but you can still recover it by resending the verification link [accounts].\n*   You must complete verification within 7 days of registration to prevent permanent deletion [accounts].\n\nSince you mentioned wanting to use loyalty points, please note that while the handbook does not specify loyalty point rules in the provided excerpts, maintaining an active and verified account is necessary to access any account-specific features or benefits.\n\n[accounts]",
    "model": "nomic-embed-text",
